    <h2>&nbsp;About Adoption</h2>
    <p>"<span class="auto-style1"><em>Adoption is not about finding children for families, it's about finding families for children"-Toyce Maguire pavao</em></span></p>

    <div class="row">
                <div class="column" style="background-color:#ccc; margin-right: 18px;">
                    <h2>Eligibility:</h2>
                    <p>--&gt;A child in India can be adopted by an Indian citizen,NRI,or a foreigner also.</p>
					<p>&nbsp;</p>
					<p>--&gt;Stable adoptive couples</p>
					<p>&nbsp;</p>
					<p>--&gt;Age difference between child and adoptive parents should not be less than 25 years.</p>
                    </div>
        <div class="column" style="background-color:#ccc; margin-right: 24px;">
           <h2>Rules:</h2>
            <p>--&gt;An adoption can be made from an orphange under the GUARDIANS AND WARDS ACT,1890, subject to court&#39;s approval.</p>
			<p>--&gt;In this case, the adoptive parents are guardians and not parents of the cild.</p>
			<p>--&gt;According to rules, Indian citizens are allowed to adopt child formally exception christians.</p>
			<p>--&gt;Adoption of children is governed by the JUVENILE JUSTICE(care and protection children)ACT,2015.</p>
        </div>
                        <div class="column" style="background-color:#ccc;">
                            <h2>Steps:</h2>
                            <p>1-Registration</p>
							<p>2-Home study and councelling</p>
							<p>3-Referral of the child</p>
							<p>4-Acceptance of the child</p>
							<p>5-Filling of petition</p>
							<p>6-Pre-adoption fostercare</p>
							<p>7-Court Hearing</p>
							<p>8-Court order</p>
							<p>9-Follow up</p>
                            </div>

